 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511746,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Kellie makes tables and chairs. Kellie profits $20 from a table (<span data-math=\"t\">t</span>), and $10 from a chair (<span data-math=\"c\">c</span>). A table requires 15 board feet of wood, while a chair requires 4 board feet of wood.  Kellie has 70 board feet available. The maximum number of tables and chairs  Kellie can make in any one day is 12. The maximum profit  Kellie can make in one day is:\n<br>\n<span data-math=\"$220\\quad\\quad{$120}\\quad\\quad{$140}\\quad\\quad{$24}\">$220\\quad\\quad{$120}\\quad\\quad{$140}\\quad\\quad{$24}</span>",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Let <i>P</i> = the profit.</p>\n<p>The profit on a table is <span data-math=\"{\\text{\\$20}}\"></span> and the profit on a chair is <span data-math=\"{\\text{\\$10}}\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"P = 20t + 10c\"></span></p>\n<p>The maximum and minimum will occur at one of the corner points. You do not need to test (0,0) because you know the profit is 0 there, even though technically it is also a corner point.</p>\n<p>Interpret.</p>\n<p>The corner points of the solution are the intersection of the two boundaries, (2, 10), and the two points: <span data-math=\"\\left( {0,12} \\right)\"></span>, and <span data-math=\"\\left( {4.\\frac{2}{3},0} \\right)\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {0,12} \\right)\"></span>What is the profit? <span data-math=\"P = 20\\left( 0 \\right) + 10\\left( {12} \\right) = \\$120\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {4.\\frac{2}{3},0} \\right)\"></span>What is the profit? <span data-math=\"P = 20\\left( {\\frac{{14}}{3}} \\right) + 10\\left( 0 \\right) \\approx \\$93.33\"></span>.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"\\left( {2,10} \\right)\"></span>What is the profit? <span data-math=\"P = 20\\left( 2 \\right) + 10\\left( {10} \\right) = \\$140\"></span>.</p>\n<p>The maximum profit is made when making 2 tables and 10 chairs. Kellie will make a profit of <span data-math=\"{\\text{\\$140}}\"></span>.</p>\n"
    },
    {
